---
id: RS-003
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: unsafe block without a // SAFETY comment
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 2

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(unsafe_block) @target'

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Add a `// SAFETY:` comment directly above this `unsafe` block naming the
invariant you are upholding (why the pointer is valid, why the bounds hold, why
the lifetime is sound). The comment is what makes the block reviewable — without
it the next edit cannot tell what must stay true.

The detector only fires when the immediately-preceding line is not already a
`// SAFETY:` comment, so a justified block is silent.
